lor":"#38bdf8","family":"Progresivo, krautrock y jazz-rock","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#canterbury"},{"id":120453583385720,"name":"Prog-rock","book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","start":1967,"end":1978,"desc":"El rock descubre los sintetizadores en su etapa de expansión; la rama progresiva los usa para investigar timbres inauditos y un sonido más complejo.","color":"#f472b6","family":"Rock, synth-pop y canción","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#prog-rock"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":262487435915763,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"Camembert Electrique","year":1971,"ess":1,"yt":"Z8c-Nl_r9Zs","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Escuela de Canterbury","scene_id":119686161909791,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#canterbury","chapters":["Sección 3.6"],"pages":[[1,63,null]]},{"id":133913635558233,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"Flying Teapot","year":1973,"ess":0,"yt":"PDDylzgr2bg","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Escuela de Canterbury","scene_id":119686161909791,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#canterbury","chapters":["Sección 3.6"],"pages":[[1,63,null]]},{"id":33802502335498,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"Angel's Egg","year":1973,"ess":1,"yt":"RXd6AAxqf7w","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Escuela de Canterbury","scene_id":119686161909791,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#canterbury","chapters":["Sección 3.6"],"pages":[[1,63,null]]},{"id":243862159519697,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"Flying Teapot (trilogía Radio Gnome Invisible)","year":1973,"ess":1,"yt":"SIgzP4Rj0Ns","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Prog-rock","scene_id":120453583385720,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#prog-rock","chapters":["Cap. 2: Rock around the click: la electrónica de los setenta, de Hallogallo al ambient en la era del Moog (1968-1982)"],"pages":[[1,53],[1,445]]},{"id":33802502335498,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"Angel’s Egg","year":1973,"ess":0,"yt":"RXd6AAxqf7w","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Prog-rock","scene_id":120453583385720,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#prog-rock","chapters":["Cap. 2: Rock around the click: la electrónica de los setenta, de Hallogallo al ambient en la era del Moog (1968-1982)"],"pages":[[1,53]]},{"id":67346351014262,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"You","year":1974,"ess":0,"yt":"H9skRFd9WLE","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Prog-rock","scene_id":120453583385720,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#prog-rock","chapters":["Cap. 2: Rock around the click: la electrónica de los setenta, de Hallogallo al ambient en la era del Moog (1968-1982)"],"pages":[]},{"id":221348199038718,"artist":"Gong","artist_id":132076427907489,"title":"You Remixed","year":1997,"ess":0,"yt":"KHWHK8Ui2vk","kind":null,"book":{"id":10,"title":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/"},"scene":"Prog-rock","scene_id":120453583385720,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/loops_timeline/#prog-rock","chapters":["Cap. 2: Rock around the click: la electrónica de los setenta, de Hallogallo al ambient en la era del Moog (1968-1982)"],"pages":[[1,54]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":61,"text":"…all other national schools. Magma (12) debuted their sci-fi concept on the ambitious and naive Magma (1970), borrowing ideas from free-jazz and Gong, and perfected it on their first masterpiece, Mekanik Destruktiw Kommandoh (1973), an eclectic and idiosyncratic rock opera that spans an amazing…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":94,"text":"…Stand By (1979) and Bolero (1979), refined the concept to manic levels. French keyboardist Cyrille Verdeaux (2) assembled a few key members of Gong (Steve Hillage, Tim Blake, Didier Malherbe) to record the Clearlight Symphony (1975), released under the moniker Clearlight, a lush electronic and…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":164,"text":"…the taste of the time via increasing nods to ambient, cosmic, new-age and ethnic music. The Magic Mushroom Band, influenced by Pink Floyd and Gong, began to emancipate themselves from their models with Process Of Illumination (1990) and ended up joining the rave scene. Mandragora's Head First…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":233,"text":"…Bright's Bright (1996) bridged Cul De Sac and shoegazing. In Florida, Meringue mixed the verve and imagination of Frank Zappa, Captain Beefheart and Gong on the monumental Music From The Mint Green Nest (1996); while Obliterati's Havy Baubaus Inflience (1998) sounded like a meeting of the Art Bears…"},{"book":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","page":242,"text":"…guitar behind Acid Mothers Temple & The Melting Paraiso U.F.O. (3). Synthesizer-heavy progressive jams in the vein of freaks such as Magma and Gong filled their early albums, Acid Mothers Temple & The Melting Paraiso Ufo (1997) and Pataphysical Freak Out Mu (1999), but subsequent collections…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":43,"text":"…veces, sus instrumentos tradicionales por el sampler, la caja de ritmos o el teclado digital. Steve Hillage, por ejemplo, pasó de ser guitarrista de Gong a estar al frente del grupo ambient-house System 7 con Miquette Giraudy; Jaki Liebezeit, batería de Can, fusionó en su última etapa percusión…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":53,"text":"…receptores. Paralelamente, Blake desarrolló una carrera en solitario como teclista planeador que tanto podía recordar a los vericuetos astrales de Gong, Ozric Tentacles o Hawkwind como parecerse a los devaneos sintetizados del francés Jean-Michel Jarre —por aquella época pasó de discreto músico…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":54,"text":"comercial rompió, en cierta medida, con la idea de que el rock es producto de un grupo y un sistema de producción. Por lo que respecta a Gong, cabe hablar de su segundo guitarrista, un Steve Hillage sinceramente interesado por la electrónica. Hillage procedía de bandas de Canterbury como…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":54,"text":"…al disco Power of Seven (1995)—, el «Hallogallo» de Neu!: toda una declaración de intenciones. Este cruce entre la música cósmica de los tiempos de Gong y el techno avanzado estaría en la base del disco de remezclas You Remixed (1997), en el que The Orb, The Shamen, 808 State, Ken Ishii y Astralasia…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":211,"text":"…fuerte, articulado alrededor de concentraciones en los monolitos prehistóricos de Stonehenge y festivales libres en los que solían tocar bandas como Gong o Hawkwind), el paso lógico en los ochenta era que el hippismo veterano abrazara la cultura del ocio como un medio para ahondar en su comunidad…"},{"book":"Loops 1 y 2. Una historia de la música electrónica","author":"Javier Blánquez (ed.)","page":365,"text":"…perdurado en el tiempo, podría haber sido un interesante puente entre la escena culta y el pujante rock progresivo — Viaje apareció en la colección Gong del sello Movieplay, dedicada al prog—, rol que, de facto, adoptó Polonio, el único de los compositores serios que participó del underground y fue…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[],"concerts":[],"xref":[],"charts":[{"id":278061142602856,"type":"album","name":"Magick Brother","list_id":116078530059197,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Canterbury Scene","src":"musthear","rank":95,"year":1970,"note":null,"yt":"8Y_rx2PZSn8","scaruffi":null},{"id":262487435915763,"type":"album","name":"Camembert Electrique","list_id":150689015758751,"list":"Genres only music snobs know about @LadoB","src":"musthear","rank":6,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"Z8c-Nl_r9Zs","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":262487435915763,"type":"album","name":"Camembert Electrique","list_id":116078530059197,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Canterbury Scene","src":"musthear","rank":25,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"Z8c-Nl_r9Zs","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":262487435915763,"type":"album","name":"Camembert Electrique","list_id":185548171992260,"list":"RYM Top — Rock — Psychedelic Rock","src":"musthear","rank":168,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"Z8c-Nl_r9Zs","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":262487435915763,"type":"album","name":"Camembert Electrique","work_year":1971,"list_id":65232636722211,"list":"Scaruffi 1970s","src":"charts","rank":309,"year":1971,"note":null,"yt":"Z8c-Nl_r9Zs","scaruffi":7.0},{"id":133913635558233,"type":"album","name":"Flying Teapot","list_id":128298934021735,"list":"RYM Top — Psychedelia","src":"musthear","rank":171,"year":1973,"note":null,"yt":"69FTdcpwpLw","